# S-PUBLISH 06. A `--workspace` name resolves, is validated, and is then dropped on the floor:
# defect: publish reports nothing to swap and swaps nothing, for a workspace that is right there.
#
# WHY THIS SHAPE. It is 05 read the other way up. 05 keeps the named target and adds others;
# this keeps the refusal and loses the target. Between them, "named means exactly these" is
# pinned from both sides, and neither red can be produced by the other defect.
#
# THE PAIRED RED (plan 5.3):
#
#   named_target_is_swapped: FAIL published ...; no daemon running to swap
#
# (that ancestor is `renamed` rather than `moved`: it matched the `swapping alpha` line, which is
# a statement of INTENT printed before the call, so what it really asserted is that alpha was
# SELECTED. The name is the honest one now; the assertion is unchanged. See moves\s-publish.tsv.)
#
# expects-red: unit:Dodona.Tests.PublishPlanTests.named_target_is_selected
#
# The controls. The absences this defect makes vacuously true must still be checked by something
# that can see the difference -- they pass here, and 05 is where they are proved to have teeth.
#
# expects-green: unit:Dodona.Tests.PublishPlanTests.unnamed_workspace_is_untouched
# expects-green: unit:Dodona.Tests.PublishPlanTests.unknown_target_is_refused
